      <div type="clause" n="75.1[a]">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Abt">Abt</ref> 75.1[a]</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="75.1[a]" corresp="#wit-h">Ðare oþre XX scll',</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#oliver" n="74.1" corresp="#wit-h">Ðare oþre, XX scƚƚ.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#oliver" corresp="#wit-h">[For a widow] of the second [rank], 20 shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-h">For violation of the <hi rend="italic">mund</hi> of a widow of the second class, 20 shillings;</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock" corresp="#wit-h">that over one of the second class, with 20 shillings; over one of the third class, with 12 shillings; over one of the fourth, with six shillings.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">[das] über die [an Range] zweite mit 20 Schll.,</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">[that] over the second [in rank] with 20 shillings,</ab>
        <note type="translator" source="#whitelock">Whitelock translates Abt 75.1 as one clause, which the sheet divides into rows 75.1[a], 75.1[b], 75.1[c]; her translation of the whole is given here, in the first row.</note>
      </div>
